1115
00:46:45,167 --> 00:46:46,800
(all chuckling)

1116
00:46:46,800 --> 00:46:50,733
- These two were in True
West for many years.

1117
00:46:50,733 --> 00:46:52,500
- I think I see a big
jackrabbit back there,

1118
00:46:52,500 --> 00:46:54,233
I'm gonna focus on that.

1119
00:46:54,233 --> 00:46:56,200
- Interesting country,
the High Desert.

1120
00:46:56,200 --> 00:46:57,400
You'd think it was
pretty lifeless

1121
00:46:57,400 --> 00:46:58,967
but there's actually
a lot going on.

1122
00:46:58,967 --> 00:47:00,433
- You know, I'd like to
hear about it some time.

1123
00:47:00,433 --> 00:47:01,833
- Oh, well we've got time now!

1124
00:47:01,833 --> 00:47:03,700
- (chuckling) We should
probably get back to the movie.

1125
00:47:03,700 --> 00:47:05,933
- Oh, I suppose you're right.

1126
00:47:05,933 --> 00:47:09,700
♪ I shot the Meo but I
didn't shoot the other guy ♪

1127
00:47:09,700 --> 00:47:11,767
♪ Do do do do do ♪

1128
00:47:11,767 --> 00:47:13,967
- Is that Fish's wife typing?

1129
00:47:13,967 --> 00:47:15,167
- Denise!

1130
00:47:15,167 --> 00:47:16,833
- What're you doin',
typin' an album?

1131
00:47:16,833 --> 00:47:18,700
- Banging away as usual, sir.

1132
00:47:18,700 --> 00:47:21,500
- Oh, that's funny
every morning.

1133
00:47:21,500 --> 00:47:23,300
- This movie packs
the unflinching humor

1134
00:47:23,300 --> 00:47:25,133
of a Dik Browne panel.

1135
00:47:26,567 --> 00:47:28,467
- Hey look, he's got
electric paneling!

1136
00:47:28,467 --> 00:47:30,533
(typing)

1137
00:47:32,133 --> 00:47:33,300
- Well.

1138
00:47:33,300 --> 00:47:34,800
- Hm.

1139
00:47:34,800 --> 00:47:36,733
- Hey, the other car in town!

1140
00:47:36,733 --> 00:47:38,900
- I think they were going
for a Touch of Evil feel

1141
00:47:38,900 --> 00:47:42,133
but they got a touch
